A||N||4||polomeno||E-Brake problem .. pls help !||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||10-11-2000||09:37 AM||||Hey guys.. I went to reconnect my E-Brakes yestarday they were very stiff.. the brake will tighten just fine on both wheels but when i release the brake they dont go all the way back , i have to move the lever on the caliper back myself , they seem to be working but just too stiff.. anything i can do to make them move more smoothly??<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||10-11-2000||09:40 AM||||Are the levers stiff if the cables are not attached?  If not then it seems that the cables may be rusted up inside the sheathes causing them to bind.||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||10-11-2000||09:45 AM||||the calipers are new .. so it is most likley the cables rusted up inside.. anything i can do for this? lube em up or something??<BR>hehe<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-11-2000||10:04 AM||||I just started working on the e-brake on my new 85GT.  The cable is siezed up solid.  I removed the lr tire so I could get to the cable.  I've been spraying it down with WD-40 and flexing it to try and loosen it up.  It is starting to brake loose.  I can pull on the parking brake lever and get it to pull a bit of slack.  I left it last night with a lot of tension on the lever hoping that it will eventually brake loose.||||reg||1
Z||000004||862M4inCA||10-11-2000||05:07 PM||||I just repaired my parking brake this last weekend and also had sticky cables. Just used a little WD-40 and worked the cables back and forth until they seemed to feel pretty good. Also, just a thought, you DO have the return springs on each caliper right? Mine didn't and I could engauge the brake, and when I went to release it, they would stay engauged. Had to run to the bone yard and finally found ONE fiero that still had the springs. Put em on, and all has been fine since.||||reg||1
